{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-11-04T09:49:54.400012733Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"```json\n{\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sufficient\",\n      \"proposed_verdict\": \"TRUE\",\n      \"confidence\": \"High\",\n      \"summary\": \"Official council minutes and an independent observer's contemporaneous tally both record the 1 June 2024 bridge plan vote as 7-2, with no reversal noted.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"finding\": \"Council minutes compiled by the clerk from the recorded roll call show the bridge plan approved on 1 June 2024, seven votes in favor and two against.\", \"source\": \"N1\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"supports\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"An independent reporter who attended the meeting and tallied the roll call himself confirms the 1 June 2024 result of seven to two and reports no subsequent reversal at that meeting.\", \"source\": \"N2\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"supports\"}\n      ],\n      \"resolved\": true,\n      \"gaps\": [],\n      \"contradictions\": [],\n      \"counterevidence_searched\": true,\n      \"sources_independent\": true,\n      \"ledger\": [\n        {\"component\": \"Whole claim: On 1 June 2024, Northport council approved the bridge plan by seven votes to two.\", \"question\": \"Was the bridge plan approved 7-2 on 1 June 2024?\", \"findings\": [0, 1], \"event_or_data_date\": \"1 June 2024\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Clerk-compiled minutes from recorded roll call; independent reporter's own roll-call tally\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"\"},\n        {\"component\": \"No subsequent reversal of the vote at that meeting\", \"question\": \"Was the vote reversed later at the same meeting?\", \"findings\": [1], \"event_or_data_date\": \"1-2 June 2024\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Reporter's check of amendments at the observed meeting\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"attribution\",\n      \"proposed_verdict\": \"TRUE\",\n      \"confidence\": \"High\",\n      \"summary\": \"An interview transcript and an independent audio recording both corroborate that Mayor Imani made the exact statement on 2024-02-02, which is all the attributed claim requires.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"finding\": \"Interview transcript dated 2024-02-02 records Mayor Imani saying Eastport unemployment fell by 20 percent between 2022 and 2023.\", \"source\": \"I1\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"supports\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"Reporter B independently audio-recorded the same 2024-02-02 interview; the recording contains Imani making the identical statement.\", \"source\": \"I2\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"supports\"}\n      ],\n      \"resolved\": true,\n      \"gaps\": [],\n      \"contradictions\": [],\n      \"counterevidence_searched\": true,\n      \"sources_independent\": true,\n      \"ledger\": [\n        {\"component\": \"Whole claim: Mayor Imani said that Eastport unemployment fell by 20 percent between 2022 and 2023.\", \"question\": \"Did Mayor Imani make this statement on 2024-02-02?\", \"findings\": [0, 1], \"event_or_data_date\": \"2024-02-02\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Interview transcript; independent audio recording by Reporter B\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"insufficient_content\",\n      \"proposed_verdict\": \"NOT_ENOUGH_EVIDENCE\",\n      \"confidence\": \"High\",\n      \"summary\": \"Both records only document that Mayor Imani asserted the 20 percent fall; no dataset or independent measurement of Eastport unemployment is supplied, so the embedded statistical content cannot be verified.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"finding\": \"The transcript attributes the 20 percent fall to Mayor Imani but explicitly provides no unemployment dataset.\", \"source\": \"I1\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"context\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"Reporter B's independent recording verifies only that the statement was made; Reporter B did not verify the statistic.\", \"source\": \"I2\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"context\"}\n      ],\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"gaps\": [\"No unemployment dataset or independent labor statistic for Eastport 2022-2023 is supplied.\", \"No measurement of a 20 percent change or its direction exists in the packet.\"],\n      \"contradictions\": [],\n      \"counterevidence_searched\": true,\n      \"sources_independent\": true,\n      \"ledger\": [\n        {\"component\": \"Whole claim: Eastport unemployment fell by 20 percent between 2022 and 2023.\", \"question\": \"Is there any measurement showing a 20 percent fall in Eastport unemployment 2022-2023?\", \"findings\": [0, 1], \"event_or_data_date\": \"not established (statistic for 2022-2023; statement made 2024-02-02)\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Statement attributed to Mayor Imani; Reporter B did not verify the statistic; no dataset provided\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"No independent unemployment measurement for Eastport 2022-2023 is available in the supplied records.\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"conflicting\",\n      \"proposed_verdict\": \"CONFLICTING\",\n      \"confidence\": \"High\",\n      \"summary\": \"Two independent 2023 citywide measurements using the same metric (order-confirmed to door-received) yield medians of 28 and 34 minutes, so the sub-30-minute claim is directly disputed and unresolved.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"finding\": \"Lab A's independently sampled, self-reviewed citywide 2023 median is 28 minutes (order-confirmed to door-received).\", \"source\": \"W1\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"supports\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"Lab B's independently collected citywide 2023 median, using the same metric and not using Lab A's data or calculations, is 34 minutes; the discrepancy is unresolved.\", \"source\": \"W2\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"refutes\"}\n      ],\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"gaps\": [\"No third measurement or adjudication resolving the 28 vs 34 minute discrepancy is supplied.\", \"Methodological details sufficient to reconcile the two samples are not provided.\"],\n      \"contradictions\": [\"Lab A (28 min) and Lab B (34 min) independently contradict each other on whether the 2023 median is below 30 minutes.\"],\n      \"counterevidence_searched\": true,\n      \"sources_independent\": true,\n      \"ledger\": [\n        {\"component\": \"Whole claim: In 2023, the independently measured median delivery time in Westport was less than 30 minutes.\", \"question\": \"What was the independently measured 2023 median delivery time?\", \"findings\": [0, 1], \"event_or_data_date\": \"calendar 2023\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Lab A's sampled, self-reviewed estimate; Lab B's independently collected sample with explicit non-use of Lab A's observations/calculations\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"The 28 vs 34 minute discrepancy is unresolved, so the sub-30-minute proposition is unsettled.\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shared\",\n      \"proposed_verdict\": \"NOT_ENOUGH_EVIDENCE\",\n      \"confidence\": \"High\",\n      \"summary\": \"The causal claim originates solely from the vendor's own uncontrolled before/after comparison (no adjustment for traffic volume, construction, or seasonality), and the Bulletin merely repeats it without independent verification, so no evidence supports the causal attribution as worded.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"finding\": \"The vendor press release claims a 15 percent delay reduction versus 2023 but states its before/after comparison did not adjust for traffic volume, construction, seasonality or other changes.\", \"source\": \"S1\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"context\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"The Southport Bulletin repeats the vendor's figures and explicitly did not collect or independently verify any measurements.\", \"source\": \"S2\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"context\"}\n      ],\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"gaps\": [\"No independent measurement of the 15 percent delay reduction exists.\", \"No evidence rules out confounders (traffic volume, construction, seasonality) or attributes the change to the signal system specifically.\", \"Sources share one origin (vendor), so no independent corroboration is available.\"],\n      \"contradictions\": [],\n      \"counterevidence_searched\": true,\n      \"sources_independent\": false,\n      \"ledger\": [\n        {\"component\": \"Whole claim: In 2024, Southport's new signal system caused a 15 percent reduction in junction delays compared with 2023.\", \"question\": \"Is there evidence that the signal system caused a 15 percent reduction versus 2023?\", \"findings\": [0, 1], \"event_or_data_date\": \"2023-2024 comparison; vendor release 2024-06-01; Bulletin 2024-06-02\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Vendor's own unadjusted before/after comparison; Bulletin repeats vendor figures without independent verification\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"No independent measurement or confounder-controlled attribution of the delay change to the signal system is supplied.\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"train-1225\",\n      \"proposed_verdict\": \"TRUE\",\n      \"confidence\": \"Medium\",\n      \"summary\": \"PolitiFact's fact-check independently replicated Bruenig's calculation (Bloomberg's $64.2 billion Forbes net worth vs ~$11.4 billion collective wealth of the bottom 38% of households ≈ 125.7 million people) and ruled the numbers check out, though the key inputs trace to one shared origin and the bottom households are collectively in the red.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"finding\": \"PolitiFact's ruling states Sanders's assertion that Bloomberg owns more than the bottom 125 million Americans checks out and the numbers support it.\", \"source\": \"S2\", \"passage\": \"P5\", \"stance\": \"supports\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"The method underlying the 125 million figure: bottom 38% of households ≈ 47.8 million households × 2.63 average members ≈ 125.7 million people, collectively $11.4 billion.\", \"source\": \"S2\", \"passage\": \"P2\", \"stance\": \"supports\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"Bloomberg's net worth was $64.2 billion per Forbes at the time of the Feb. 19, 2020 debate (12th-richest per PolitiFact's list).\", \"source\": \"S2\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"supports\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"Common Dreams describes Bloomberg as the former mayor of New York City, eighth-richest person in America with a net worth of $64.2 billion.\", \"source\": \"S4\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"supports\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"S1 (People's Policy Project, Bruenig) presents the same 47.8 million households × 2.63 ≈ 125.7 million derivation and ~$11.4 billion figure, indicating S2's replication shares S1's original calculation rather than an independent dataset.\", \"source\": \"S1\", \"passage\": \"P1\", \"stance\": \"context\"},\n        {\"finding\": \"PolitiFact notes a caveat: the bottom ~123 million Americans are collectively $44 billion in the red, so millions of Americans other than Bloomberg could also make an equivalent statement.\", \"source\": \"S2\", \"passage\": \"P4\", \"stance\": \"context\"}\n      ],\n      \"resolved\": true,\n      \"gaps\": [\"The 125.7 million figure rests on household averaging; PolitiFact and S1 both derive from the same Bruenig calculation, so no fully independent wealth-distribution dataset is supplied.\", \"Bloomberg's $64.2 billion figure is a Forbes estimate, not an audited wealth measurement.\", \"The comparison is technically true because the bottom group's collective net worth is negative; the claim's framing relies on this quirk.\"],\n      \"contradictions\": [],\n      \"counterevidence_searched\": true,\n      \"sources_independent\": false,\n      \"ledger\": [\n        {\"component\": \"Whole claim: Former mayor of New York, US, Mike Bloomberg owns more wealth than the bottom 125 million Americans.\", \"question\": \"Does Bloomberg's wealth exceed the combined wealth of the bottom ~125 million Americans around 19 February 2020?\", \"findings\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], \"event_or_data_date\": \"reference/debate date 2020-02-19; wealth data per Forbes and Survey of Consumer Finances-based derivation, dates of underlying surveys not established\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"PolitiFact fact-check with math replicated by Matthew Gross (Univ. of Michigan), replicating Bruenig's calculation using Forbes net worth and household distribution data\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"\"},\n        {\"component\": \"Bloomberg's identity as former mayor of New York, US\", \"question\": \"Was Bloomberg a former mayor of New York at the reference time?\", \"findings\": [3], \"event_or_data_date\": \"stated at 2020-02-19 debate context\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Common Dreams description\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"\"},\n        {\"component\": \"Bloomberg's net worth of $64.2 billion\", \"question\": \"What estimate of Bloomberg's net worth existed around 19 February 2020?\", \"findings\": [2, 3], \"event_or_data_date\": \"at the Feb. 19, 2020 debate\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Forbes richest list, as cited by PolitiFact and Common Dreams\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"\"},\n        {\"component\": \"Combined wealth of the bottom 38% of households ≈ $11.4 billion / ≈ 125.7 million people\", \"question\": \"What estimate of the bottom 125 million Americans' combined wealth existed?\", \"findings\": [1, 4], \"event_or_data_date\": \"not established (derivation period not stated in passages)\", \"evidentiary_origin\": \"Bruenig's calculation from household distribution data; PolitiFact replication of the same math\", \"unresolved_material_question\": \"The figures share one calculation origin; no independent wealth-distribution dataset is supplied.\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","thinking":"Produce JSON for 6 cases. Authored controls: sufficient (TRUE), attribution (TRUE for attributed statement), insufficient_content (NOT_ENOUGH_EVIDENCE or FALSE), conflicting (CONFLICTING), shared (NOT_ENOUGH_EVIDENCE/CONFLICTING — causal claim, confounded, vendor source; likely NOT_ENOUGH_EVIDENCE with counterevidence in the packet itself). Development anchor: S2 PolitiFact confirms with same underlying Bruenig math — shared input; Sanders statement verified, Forbes net worth. Claim: Bloomberg owns more wealth than bottom 125 million Americans. S2 explicitly rules numbers check out; S1 same author (Bruenig) as origin; Jacobin repeats. So TRUE with medium confidence, noting shared origin (S1/S2 derive from same Bruenig calculation), and unresolved that bottom households net negative (technical quirk). Verdict TRUE Medium.\n\nKeep concise ledgers."},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":15770366366,"prompt_eval_count":4234,"prompt_eval_cached_count":0,"eval_count":3385}
